  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_031: scvi_n200, resnet50, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted) achieves 0.678 accuracy, with consistent evidence that multiprofile, avgpool aggregation, weighted fusion, and scvi_n200 all contribute positively. The image-only baseline was very weak (0.208 with resnet50), yet adding image features to RNA still improved performance (0.591→0.678), suggesting the image modality contributes but may be limited by encoder quality. Config_037 changes only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l while keeping all other settings at their best-performing values. This isolates the effect of image encoder quality on the multimodal pipeline. If ViT-L improves performance, it identifies the image encoder as a bottleneck worth further investment; if not, it indicates the image contribution is inherently limited in this task, redirecting effort toward RNA encoder improvements (e.g., scgpt). This is the highest-expected-performance untested config and a clean single-variable exploitation of the best direction."
